## Ingredients

- 2 boneless chicken breasts, thawed and sliced into strips
- 1 can (13.5 oz) coconut milk
- 5 tsp Maesri panang curry paste
- 2 cups chicken stock
- 2 medium carrots, sliced into thin half-moons
- 1/4 cup roasted peanuts, chopped
- 1 tbsp neutral oil
- 1 tsp brown sugar
- Juice of 1/2 lime
- Fish sauce, to taste (optional)
- Thai basil (optional)

## Steps

1. In a large pot over medium-high, sear the chicken in oil, 2 to 3 minutes per side. Set aside.
2. Lower heat to medium. In the same pot, fry the paste in the thick cream from the top of the coconut milk until fragrant.
3. Add the rest of the coconut milk and the stock, scraping up the browned bits. Add the carrots and simmer until just tender.
4. Return the chicken and simmer until cooked through (165°F).
5. Stir in sugar and lime juice, and adjust to taste.
6. Top with peanuts (and basil if using). Serve over rice.

